{"abstract":"AIM: This study explores the hands-on experiences and perspectives of general practice staff regarding the feasibility of conducting artificial intelligence-assisted (AI-assisted) diabetic retinopathy screenings (DRS) in general practice settings. METHOD: The screenings were tested in 12 general practices in the North Denmark Region and were conducted as part of daily care routines over ~4 weeks. Subsequently, 21 staff members involved in the DRS were interviewed. RESULTS: Thematic analysis generated four main themes: (1) Experiences with DRS in daily practice, (2) Effective DRS implementation in general practice in the future, (3) Trust and approval of AI-assisted DRS in general practice, and (4) Implications of DRS in general practice. The findings suggest that general practice staff recognise the potential for AI-assisted DRS to be integrated into their clinical workflows. However, they also emphasise the importance of addressing both practical and systemic factors to ensure successful implementation of DRS within the general practice setting. CONCLUSION: Focusing on the practical experiences and perspectives of general practice staff, this study lays the groundwork for future research aimed at optimising the implementation of AI-assisted DRS in general practice settings, while recognising that the insights gained may also inform broader primary care contexts.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Krogh, Malene","Hentze, Malene","Jensen, Morten Sig Ager","Jensen, Martin Bach","Nielsen, Marie Germund","Vorum, Henrik","Kristensen, Jette Kolding"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805100"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Krogh, Malene"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Machine learning","Primary care","Qualitative Research","Stakeholder perspectives","diabetic retinopathy screening"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"valuable insights into general practice staff s experiences and perspectives on ai assisted diabetic retinopathy screening an interview study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmed.2025.1565532","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The author(s) declare financial support was received for the research, authorship, and/or publication of this article. This study received funding from Steno Diabetes Center North Denmark, the Vissing Foundation, the Organisation of General Practitioners in Denmark, and Nord-KAP."],"id":"S01-000.00-805100","identifier":[{"id":"40134918","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105001023964","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11933039","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-6ff8f916-20f1-435e-bf3b-0e02b2211692"],"keyword":["Artificial Intelligence","Machine Learning","Primary Care","Qualitative Research","diabetic retinopathy screening","stakeholder perspectives"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C42145B84B3710A860AABCB8E348AC12"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmed.2025.1565532","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/772629016/fmed-1-1565532.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Center for General Practice at Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Malene","key":"kroghmalenepau","last":"Krogh","locid":"d192dd43-5f01-4ffe-bf2f-bfe353892bdf","name":"Krogh, Malene","orcid":"0000-0003-2790-1020","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene","key":"hentzemalenepau","last":"Hentze","locid":"c34f655e-ce89-45a8-a99a-6812b28c8779","name":"Hentze, Malene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Sig Ager","key":"jensenmortensigagerpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"de4051ce-fce4-4bfc-b3b7-b215597e93c4","name":"Jensen, Morten Sig Ager","orcid":"0000-0002-3075-882X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Bach","key":"jensenmartinbachpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"929fc31a-f5b6-45b8-b3ed-29bd2c4b4bf7","name":"Jensen, Martin Bach","orcid":"0000-0003-2162-7390","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Germund","key":"nielsenmariegermundpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"da949407-1978-46cd-b64a-06f903c65ffc","name":"Nielsen, Marie Germund","orcid":"0000-0001-7048-6294","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"vorumhenrikpau","last":"Vorum","locid":"60554352-1557-4c7b-905d-e4b7c7f8c94a","name":"Vorum, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-7600-0731","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jette","key":"kristensenjettekoldingpau","last":"Kolding Kristensen","locid":"4e8e0768-5c50-4b43-823c-dc0467cb2b01","name":"Kristensen, Jette Kolding","name_org":"Kolding Kristensen, Jette","orcid":"0000-0002-2648-5750","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40134918"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fmed.2025.1565532","issn":["2296858X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Medicine","paperid":"1565532","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Medicine","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105001023964"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6ff8f916-20f1-435e-bf3b-0e02b2211692"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Valuable insights into general practice staff's experiences and perspectives on AI-assisted diabetic retinopathy screening-An interview study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-805100","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: The aim of this study is to explore general practice staff perspectives regarding a teaching concept based on instructional videos for conducting DR screenings. Furthermore, this study aims to investigate the competencies acquired by the staff through this teaching concept. DESIGN AND SETTING: Qualitative cross-sectional study conducted in general practice clinics in the North Denmark Region. METHOD: A teaching concept was developed based on instruction videos to teach general practice staff to conduct diabetic retinopathy screenings with automated grading through artificial intelligence. Semi-structured interviews were performed with 16 staff members to investigate their perspectives on the concept and acquired competencies. RESULTS: This study found no substantial resistance to the teaching concept from staff; however, participants' satisfaction with the methods employed in the instruction session, the progression of learning curves, screening competencies, and their acceptance of a known knowledge gap during screenings varied slightly among the participants. CONCLUSION: This study showed that the teaching concept can be used to teach general practice staff to conduct diabetic retinopathy screenings. Staffs' perspectives on the teaching concept and acquired competencies varied, and this study suggest few adjustments to the concept to accommodate staff's preferences and establish more consistent competencies.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Krogh, Malene","Jensen, Martin Bach","Jensen, Morten Sig Ager","Hentze, Malene","Nielsen, Marie Germund","Vorum, Henrik","Kristensen, Jette Kolding"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-757108"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Krogh, Malene"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","General practice","Qualitative Research","Teaching","Type 2 diabetes","Video","diabetic retinopathy screening"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring general practice staff perspectives on a teaching concept based on instruction videos for diabetic retinopathy screening an interview study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/02813432.2024.2396873","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study and three following studies with the aim of testing the feasibility of DR screenings with automated grading in Danish general practices for patients with T2D are funded by Steno Diabetes Center North Denmark, Vissing Foundation, Organisation of General Practitioners in Denmark and Nord-KAP."],"id":"S01-000.00-757108","identifier":[{"id":"85203000086","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39225788","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-a33c3344-daf2-4e6f-a705-688e078c19e9"],"keyword":["Type 2 diabetes","artificial intelligence","diabetic retinopathy screening","general practice","qualitative research","teaching","video"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D572E6C758CE6D7867292853A2774DE0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/02813432.2024.2396873","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/773234846/Krogh_et_al._2025_._Exploring_general_practice_staff_perspectives_on_a_teaching_concept_based_on_instruction_videos_for_diabetic_retinopathy_screening_an_interview_study.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg Univ