{"abstract":"Low back pain (LBP) is a major health issue globally. Self-management, including evidence-based treatment components such as patient education, exercise and advice to remain active, is consistently recommended in LBP clinical guidelines. Delivery of self-management through digital platforms, such as mobile applications (apps) is hypothesized as supportive for patients when managing their condition.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Sandal, Louise Fleng","Stochkendahl, Mette Jensen","Kjaer, Per","Hartvigsen, Jan","Nicholl, Barbara I","Mair, Frances S","Wood, Karen","Nilsen, Tom Ivar Lund","Villumsen, Morten","Rasmussen, Charlotte Diana Nørregaard","Svendsen, Malene Jagd","Cooper, Kay","Bach, Kerstin","Mork, Paul Jarle","Søgaard, Karen"],"cuid":["S02-084.68-049370"],"event":{"end":"2019-03-23","place":"Berlin, de","start":"2019-03-20","title":"15th Wo´rld Federation of Chiropractic Biennial Congress . 78th European Chiropractors Union Convention","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","Robert Gordon University","St. Olav University Hospital","The Robert Gordon´s University (Formerly Robert Gordon´s Institute of Technology), Aberdeen, Scotland","University of Glasgow"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"OT":["Norwegian Technical and Natural Science University"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effectiveness of an app delivered self management program for persons with low back pain protocol for the selfback randomised controlled 