{"abstract":"Background: Cyclooxygenase (COX) activity is increased in endoscopic normal colonic mucosa from patients with colorectal neoplasia (CRN). COX-2 is thought to be the predominant COX isozyme involved in neoplasia. Meanwhile, relative contributions of COX-1 and COX-2 isoforms are unknown. Knowledge about their mutual activity in colonic mucosa is important for diagnostics and targeted therapy for CRN. The aim of this study was to assess the relative function, expression and localization of COX-1 and COX-2 enzymes in colonic non-neoplastic human mucosa and thereby to potentially reveal a mucosal disease predisposition for better treatment. Methods: Biopsies were pinched from normal appearing colonic mucosa in patients undergoing endoscopy. Ussing chamber technique was applied for an indirect assessment of epithelial activity, RT-qPCR for expression and immunohistochemistry for localization of COX-1 and COX-2 enzymes in patients without (ctrls) and with a history of CRN (CRN-pts). Results: Combined COX-1 and COX-2 activity was higher in CRN-pts, p=0.036. COX-2 was primarily localized in absorptive cells, while COX-1 appeared to be restricted to nonenteroendocrine tuft cells of the colonic epithelium. Conclusions: In biopsies from endoscopic normal appearing colonic mucosa, combined activity of COX-1 and COX-2 enzymes is increased in CRN-pts compared with ctrls. This indicates that COX-1 and COX-2 together contribute to an increased proliferation process. Of note, in colonic epithelial cell lining, the COX-1 enzyme seems localized in tuft cells.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jensen, Thorbjørn Søren Rønn","Mahmood, Badar","Damm, Morten Bach","Backe, Marie Balslev","Dahllöf, Mattias Salling","Poulsen, Steen Seier","Hansen, Mark Berner","Bindslev, Niels"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-523249"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Biopsy","Carcinogenesis","Cyclooxygenase","Endoscopic","Tuft cells"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"combined activity of cox 000000000001 and cox 000000000002 is increased in non neoplastic colonic mucosa from colorectal neoplasia patients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12876-018-0759-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-523249","identifier":[{"id":"29486731","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85042566407","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5830335","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-d955efa5-fcae-410c-b02a-c1d36901d9f8"],"keyword":["Biopsy","Carcinogenesis","Cyclooxygenase","Endoscopic","Short circuit current (SCC)","Tuft cells"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F6E0DDB7F881A8AF2286E5EF1AF835F5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12876-018-0759-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/215928253/s12876_018_0759_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Thorbjørn Søren Rønn","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Thorbjørn Søren Rønn","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Badar","key":"mahmoodpau","last":"Mahmood","locid":"484275c3-6f8b-402a-9177-945086caa484","name":"Mahmood, Badar","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten Bach","key":"dammpau","last":"Damm","name":"Damm, Morten Bach","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marie Balslev","key":"backepau","last":"Backe","locid":"f4af604d-c356-4633-94e8-076913cb2903","name":"Backe, Marie Balslev","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mattias Salling","key":"dahllöfpau","last":"Dahllöf","locid":"7bbe347a-9252-4271-8d66-d1b6c065479d","name":"Dahllöf, Mattias Salling","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steen Seier","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"8959d81d-fe64-4ef4-86b7-003b7b637e8e","name":"Poulsen, Steen Seier","orcid":"0000-0003-4419-4911","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mark Berner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Mark Berner","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels","key":"bindslevpau","last":"Bindslev","locid":"b34ae3f8-b3e3-4f9f-9b46-3c63a950cb4f","name":"Bindslev, Niels","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29486731"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12876-018-0759-1","issn":["1471230X"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Gastroenterology","paperid":"31","status":"p","title":"BMC Gastroenterology","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85042566407"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d955efa5-fcae-410c-b02a-c1d36901d9f8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Combined activity of COX-1 and COX-2 is increased in non-neoplastic colonic mucosa from colorectal neoplasia patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-523249","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To summarise recommendations about 20 non-surgical interventions for recent onset (<12 weeks) non-specific low back pain (LBP) and lumbar radiculopathy (LR) based on two guidelines from the Danish Health Authority. Methods: Two multidisciplinary working groups formulated recommendations based on the GRADE approach. Results: Sixteen recommendations were based on evidence, and four on consensus. Management of LBP and LR should include information about prognosis, warning signs, and advise to remain active. If treatment is needed, the guidelines suggest using patient education, different types of supervised exercise, and manual therapy. The guidelines recommend against acupuncture, routine use of imaging, targeted treatment, extraforaminal glucocorticoid injection, paracetamol, NSAIDs, and opioids. Conclusion: Recommendations are based on low to moderate quality evidence or on consensus, but are well aligned with recommendations from international guidelines. The guideline working groups recommend that research efforts in relation to all aspects of management of LBP and LR be intensified.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Stochkendahl, Mette Jensen","Kjær, Per","Hartvigsen, Jan","Kongsted, Alice","Aaboe, Jens","Andersen, Margrethe","Andersen, Mikkel Ø.","Fournier, Gilles","Højgaard, Betina","Jensen, Martin Bach","Jensen, Lone Donbæk","Karbo, Ture","Kirkeskov, Lilli","Melbye, Martin","Morsel-Carlsen, Lone","Nordsteen, Jan","Palsson, Thorvaldur Skuli","Rasti, Zoreh","Silbye, Peter Frost","Steiness, Morten Zebitz","Tarp, Simon","Vaagholt, Morten"],"cuid":["S04-095.37-004291"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"keyword":["Analgesics therapeutic use","Clinical guideline","Conservative Treatment methods","Conservative treatment","Denmark","Exercise Therapy methods","Humans","Journal Article","Low Back Pain therapy","Low back pain","Musculoskeletal Manipulations methods","Non surgical intervention","Pain Management methods","Pain Measurement","Patient Education as Topic methods","Prognosis","Radiculopathy therapy","Recommendations","Review"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Sundhedsstyrelsen"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"national clinical guidelines for non surgical treatment of patients with recent onset low back pain or lumbar radiculopathy","src":["aau","au","sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00586-017-5099-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-095.37-004291","identifier":[{"id":"85018513276","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28429142","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-57f7d601-f02a-4c54-be4b-4a88077fb47d","au-08468c1a-5f48-42e3-a0fd-dd81ab11c73f","sdu-e53d5ff1-a99e-47a6-8538-711d622f6d34","ucl-5e52b961-fff2-4d32-adbd-f059c1d5b48b"],"keyword":["Analgesics/therapeutic use","Clinical guideline","Conservative Treatment/methods","Conservative treatment","Denmark","Exercise Therapy/methods","Humans","Journal Article","Low Back Pain/therapy","Low back pain","Lumbar radiculopathy","Musculoskeletal Manipulations/methods","Non-surgical intervention","Pain Management/methods","Pain Measurement","Patient Education as Topic/methods","Prognosis","Radiculopathy/therapy","Recommendations","Review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-6F343691468C5C51BCF73228A83DFA4